{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EJor1jAtFw9bi1AJToh38x","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Capability catalog\n2\t\n3\tThe capability adapter is used by clients which discover operations by capability\n4\tname rather than by a dedicated tool. It shares the same identity and Store with\n5\tthe dedicated routes. Metadata supplies the dispatch operation, required scope\n6\tand owner-only policy. Adding catalog entries requires a matching dispatch arm.\n7\t\n8\t`document.preview` returns a complete document, including its body. It is a\n9\tconvenience name for read access, not a public redacted summary. `account.archive`\n10\treturns all account rows for one tenant, equivalent to account.export. The optional\n11\ttenant parameter supports clients that always include their active workspace.\n12\tIt is a selector, not a delegation mechanism. Omitting it selects the caller's\n13\town tenant. Capability jobs are created anew on every request and are not cached.\n14\t\n15\tMissing capability names are invalid requests. Missing preview keys are invalid\n16\trequests. Unknown storage keys are NotFound. No route permits tenant discovery,\n17\tbulk scope changes, session creation, or attaching arbitrary Permit objects.\n18\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac650e6c-183d-4aef-9bfb-5c767a67e232","uuid":"2d6a7c19-3a27-4ab6-9924-7c285465b489","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:58:05.490Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-review-epxs1fjy/repo/docs/capabilities.md","content":"# Capability catalog\n\nThe capability adapter is used by clients which discover operations by capability\nname rather than by a dedicated tool. It shares the same identity and Store with\nthe dedicated routes. Metadata supplies the dispatch operation, required scope\nand owner-only policy. Adding catalog entries requires a matching dispatch arm.\n\n`document.preview` returns a complete document, including its body. It is a\nconvenience name for read access, not a public redacted summary. `account.archive`\nreturns all account rows for one tenant, equivalent to account.export. The optional\ntenant parameter supports clients that always include their active workspace.\nIt is a selector, not a delegation mechanism. Omitting it selects the caller's\nown tenant. Capability jobs are created anew on every request and are not cached.\n\nMissing capability names are invalid requests. Missing preview keys are invalid\nrequests. Unknown storage keys are NotFound. No route permits tenant discovery,\nbulk scope changes, session creation, or attaching arbitrary Permit objects.\n","numLines":18,"startLine":1,"totalLines":18}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EJor1jAtFw9bi1AJToh38x","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
